/**
@defgroup autonomyConditions [Common] Autonomy Errors and Diagnostics
@section Description
Framework for reporting errors and diagnostics from the autonomy system

@section Detailed Description
Autonomy conditions define a base interface class consisting of a condition name, message, and optional debounce and time-to-live parameters.  The autonomy task object uses this common interface for raising, suppressing, and clearing conditions set by user code.

This module also contains a script for generating source code new conditions.  A sub-folder called "conditions" contains all of the autonomy conditions that exist within the AHS system.

